    "module": {
      "purpose": "Provides a React context, provider, hook, and portal component for rendering editor content into a dedicated DOM host at the end of the editor container.",
      "summary": "This module defines the editor portal boundary used to escape the canvas stacking layer while preserving editor-container positioning and deterministic DOM ordering. A provider supplies an optional HTMLElement through context, a hook exposes that host to consumers, and the portal component renders children into it with React DOM portals. Rendering safely produces no output until the host exists.",
      "businessContext": "Supports editor overlays such as shape annotations, popovers, comments, and panels that must paint above canvas and editor UI layers. Failure leaves anchored overlay content unrendered or incorrectly ordered in the DOM.",
